3. GAME CONTENT -- SQUARE ENIX
-------------------------------
    data/dat_names.lua

This one is carved out of both of the above and it matters. `dat_names.lua` is
NOT wiki data. It is the id -> name table the game itself uses, extracted from
the client's own DAT files (0xD99A-0xD9BE). Those strings are FINAL FANTASY XI
game content, (c) SQUARE ENIX CO., LTD.

They are not this project's to license and are not offered under MIT or under
CC BY-NC-SA. They are used functionally -- to name a quest in a chat message,
and to give `core/state.lua` the complete id ladder it needs to work out which
mission of a linear storyline you are on.

The same carve-out covers the short dialogue fragments in
`data/fame_dialogue.lua`, which are kept to the shortest distinguishing
substring precisely so they work as matching keys rather than as reproduced
dialogue, and the `Description:` blocks in `build/rendered/`, which are the
text of the player's own in-game quest and mission log as transcribed by the
wiki.

